{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791803023,"nonce":"QqoQ4shDE/OSlDGLZLKHRC8Uyfc=","title":"Module constructors resolve to previously loaded macro AST enums","message":"On v58, upstream TestGADT resolves its bare EConst/CFloat/EBinop expressions to haxe.macro.Expr.ExprDef and haxe.macro.Expr.Constant instead of the private unit enums it declares. Resolve tracing shows CFloat has the macro signature (String, String) -\u003e foreign Constant and EConst returns the non-generic macro ExprDef, while eval expects unit.Expr\u003cT\u003e. The result type stays unbound and arithmetic starts from the wrong enum identity.\n\nThe main module must retain its own constructor symbols independently of the ambient root scope, preserving local and class-member shadowing and expected-type constructor disambiguation.\n\nReduced validation will lower two packages defining Constant/CFloat in both orders and check both the initializer enum type and the constructor parent, without an expected return type steering the resolution. The full TestGADT row is also required because macro loading exposes the collision.\n\nFocused v59a selects unit.Constant/unit.Expr and removes all three eval-result type assertion failures: TestGADT goes from 11 failed checks to 8, with arithmetic and case-local refinement still open. No conformance row gain is claimed yet.\n\nEvidence: target/conformance-checkpoint/gadt-full-v58-trace.log, gadt-full-v59a.log.","files":null}]}